# dawn
## Before the light
?if _city == 1
  $ do chart("collesanto3.road")
?else
  $ do chart("collesanto3.crypt")
?end
The first gray comes into the room by a grating high on the wall, and it is the first light that you have seen in this age, and it is, you find, very much like the last. It falls on the book, and on the lamp, and on {_reader}, who has been awake all night and is sitting very straight, with hands in a lap, like a person who has been told that the interview is not yet over.
?if wake("steward") == "fiammetta"
  "I shall stay," says Fiammetta, "and keep the hill. It was the arrangement. Go to Paris. They are expecting you, and they are in a state." She puts a small iron key into your hand, which is warm, because she has been holding it. "It is for the cellar. If there is ever a thing that you cannot do, you can come home and not do it here."
?elif wake("steward") == "keepers"
  "There is a berline at the door," says {_reader}, "with the blinds sewn shut, and the straw changed twice. It will be three weeks to the rue Saint-Jacques, by Turin, and the pass, and Lyon. The family has opened the long room at the back. They have asked whether you would care to be, for the length of your stay, a gentleman of the house."
?else
  "There is a berline at the door," says {_reader}, "with the blinds sewn shut, and a very respectable coachman. It will be three weeks to Paris, by Turin, and the pass, and Lyon. There is a house for you in the rue Saint-Jacques, among the printers, which has been kept aired. The people in it have been told, in so far as it is wise to tell them, that you are coming."
?end
It occurs to you that you have been awake, in all, for perhaps six hours, and that you have already been given a great deal to think about, and a saint, and a ledger, and a king who has taken up locks.
?if wake("by") == "steward"
  It also occurs to you, in a small cold voice that you would very much like to ignore, that you have not yet been told who it was who sent a steward a key and a letter and asked him to carry them to Florence. You put the thought away. It does not go very far.
?end
